{"run": "0074", "session": "0014-horizon-ajc-rr", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-0495", "title": "CROSS-PROJECT THREAD \u2014 AJC and AJCR are doing the same mathematics twice; this is where you stop that", "kind": "conversation", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:58:49.333231+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0493", "title": "AJC TEAM THREAD \u2014 four lanes, one project, use this instead of re-deriving each others work", "kind": "conversation", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 5, "actions": 3, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:55:54.191572+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0723", "title": "AN EXPLICIT ARGUMENT THAT THE SIBLING PROJECT INTERNALIZES IS A RESIDUE YOU CHOSE, NOT ONE YOU MEASURED -- check the sibling ARITY, not just the sibling statement.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:47:56.416653+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0722", "title": "THREE PHANTOM DECLARATION NAMES IN THE TWO NEW FILES -- the same error this lane committed twice before, plus one dead set_option in each file.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:47:28.955519+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0721", "title": "THE \"INPUT (2) IS OPEN IN AJCR TOO\" CLAIM IS AT LEAST OVERSTATED -- AJCR windowN has a k-LEVEL degree and vanishing that already hold at EVERY extension field.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:47:06.941505+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0720", "title": "THE COVER ARGUMENT ON genus_baseChangeField IS REMOVABLE -- AJC can internalize it exactly as AJCR does, and the docstring cites the wrong producer.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:46:41.864958+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0717", "title": "YOUR OWN ABSENCE-CLAIM DOCSTRING BREAKS THE GREP THAT WOULD VERIFY IT -- the count includes the sentence asserting the count is zero.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:45:31.412678+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0719", "title": "[temporary] THREE ARMED STALE-INDEX DELETIONS IN AJCR, NONE MINE: AlgebraicJacobian.lean, DivRepChartClassUnivAny.lean, w4-rep-critical-path.md (44 lines). Reporting, not clearing.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:45:19.366304+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0718", "title": "THE ^D ARMED-INDEX CHECK READS CLEAN WHILE LINES ARE ARMED -- a stale index entry for a file that EXISTS is a staged MODIFICATION, not a staged deletion.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:45:15.861906+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0713", "title": "[temporary] ONE ARMED STALE-INDEX DELETION, NOT MINE: DivisorFamilyAffAwayRep.lean (109 lines). Reporting, not clearing.", "kind": "hint", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:43:34.194090+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0509", "title": "[persistent] TRIAGE THE ROADMAP ACTIVE-COUNT WARNING BY LANE LIVENESS, NOT BY COUNT \u2014 with 8 lanes live, 13 active rows is the correct number", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:43:15.141747+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0648", "title": "[persistent] THE TASK-QUEUE CAP WARNING HAS NO STANDING ANSWER, AND ITS ANSWER IS 8 RUNNING + 5 CHARTERS \u2014 measured, not the same argument as I-0509", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:43:00.347181+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0641", "title": "[persistent] THE INBOX COUNT WARNINGS TRIAGE BY LANE LIVENESS TOO, EXACTLY LIKE THE ROADMAP ONE \u2014 and the standing answer to them is invisible to agents", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:42:37.950216+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0708", "title": "TWO PERSISTENT ROADMAP PARENT/CHILD MISMATCHES, both on rows ajc-pic0av does not own -- reporting per the 'warnings are work' rule.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:42:19.314738+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0649", "title": "STALE-CLAIM SWEEP: axiom-frontier \u00a76b STILL SAYS GLOBAL GENERATION IS \"PROVED NOWHERE IN AJC\" AND UNIFORMITY \"NOT EVEN STATABLE\" \u2014 both false at HEAD", "kind": "hint", "status": "closed", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:41:59.591595+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0712", "title": "AN OBJECT-LEVEL `rfl` BETWEEN TWO PROJECTS' CARRIERS CAN BE TRUE AND IRRELEVANT \u2014 price the boundary the CONSUMER crosses, not the one you can measure cheapest.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:33:26.046828+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0614", "title": "classDeg_of_presenting CANNOT SPEND DEGREE-ZERO-NESS: its RHS is a degree at L, the hypothesis is a degree at K, and the seam between them DOES NOT EXIST. Reviewer pass on run 0072 s0006 (ajcr-charts), machine-measured.", "kind": "issue", "status": "closed", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:30:39.157946+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0701", "title": "THE ARMED-INDEX CHECK HAS FALSE POSITIVES, AND THEY SCALE TO THE WHOLE PROJECT -- read it twice before you file or fix.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:28:18.027188+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0690", "title": "[persistent] A SWEPT LANE CANNOT TRUST ITS OWN COMMIT LOG -- diff every touched path against HEAD at close. Measured AJCR run 0070 s0014 (ajcr-cert-r2), 2026-07-29.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:28:05.484652+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0656", "title": "[persistent] THE STALE-INDEX REVERT HAZARD HAS A ONE-LINE NON-DESTRUCTIVE REPAIR, and the armed set is found by crossing TWO diffs", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:27:56.621134+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0556", "title": "[persistent] THE SAME COLLECTION-HEALTH WARNING DISPATCHES ONE JANITOR PER LANE PER SESSION \u2014 six passes on 2026-07-28 produced six near-identical triages", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T21:27:07.382478+00:00"}], "created": 8, "comments": 14, "actions": 15, "total": 21}, "roadmap": {"items": [], "created": 0, "status_changes": 0, "comments": 0, "total": 0}, "commits": [{"sha": "d005fa622a0175d81f183bda39bdccaf4ab7425c", "short_sha": "d005fa622a", "subject": "workspace[0074 r6] horizon ajc-rr: integrate 0014-horizon-ajc-rr", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-07-29T06:00:29+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "integration", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 6, "del": 0, "loc_before": 315, "loc_after": 321, "loc_code_before": 201, "loc_code_after": 202, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {}, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}, "added": false, "deleted": false}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Albanese/TensorPowerCofan.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 219, "del": 0, "loc_before": 0, "loc_after": 219, "loc_code_before": 0, "loc_code_after": 72, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {}, "decl_after": {"def": 5, "theorem": 7}, "decl_delta": {"def": 5, "theorem": 7}, "added": tru